 * Description:               PROVISIONAL Liberty for AION_mux4i_1
 *
 * Function: inverting 4:1 mux:  O0 = !(I5 ? (I4 ? I3 : I2) : (I4 ? I1 : I0))
 *
 * Area is the FLOORPLAN.md width (or a trial value), not a drawn cell -- 17 CoreSites x 1.8144 um2 =
 * 30.8448 um2 -- against a PDK baseline of sg13g2_mux4_1 + sg13g2_inv_1, 24 sites.
 * FLOORPLAN.md: 9 columns, 4 diffusion breaks (the minimum) each widened
 * by 120 nm, Activ 7810 nm in 8160 nm; drawn and verified at this width.
 * It is the number ABC chooses on, so it is the knob to sweep: the largest
 * site count at which the mapper still takes the cell is the layout budget.
 *
 * Every timing and power table is sg13g2_mux4_1's unconditional arc,
 * copied verbatim with related_pin renamed (I0 <- A0, I1 <- A1, I2 <- A2, I3 <- A3, I4 <- S0, I5 <- S1).
 * Its conditional (`when`) arcs and state-dependent leakage are dropped,
 * because their conditions name the donor's pins.  cell_leakage_power is
 * the donor's scaled by device count (464.975 nW x 18/26).
 * Static-mux tables flatter a data path through two TGs; characterize
 * with --driver-cell before believing any of it.
 *
 * It is NOT a characterization.  scripts/pdk_cell.py's post-layout stage
 * writes the .lib that replaces it; never sign anything off against this.
 * ================================================================ */
